<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trailokyachandra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trailokyachandra was a king of the Chandra dynasty of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> in the early 10th century. Starting from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harikela">Harikela</a> and Chandradvipa, he extended his rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanga">Vanga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samatata">Samatata</a>, laying the foundations of the kingdom inherited by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrichandra">Shrichandra</a>. He is known from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate inscriptions of his successors.</p></div>
